## Audit conclusion

Phase 1.5 remains **in progress**. Repository implementation and closure hardening are present, but the master completion gate requires candidate-bound publication evidence and real external evidence that code and fixtures cannot manufacture.

`npm run phase15:audit:local` reports only `localReady`. `npm run ci:prepublish` produces `publicationReady` for the exact candidate SHA. `npm run phase15:audit` intentionally exits nonzero until `localReady`, `publicationReady`, and `externalReady` are all true. The closure sentence is emitted only by the latter command.

`localReady` never authorizes publication. `publicationReady` never claims GitHub/provider/deployment evidence. A changed SHA invalidates candidate-bound evidence.

## Increment status

| Increment | Repository state | Evidence state |
|---|---|---|
| M1 — contracts and governance | Implemented | Eight roles and source hashes validate |
| PR-A — telemetry foundation | Implemented | Schema, redaction, normalization, sink, and failure tests pass |
| PR-B — context preflight/compiler | Implemented | Determinism, reference-first, deduplication, exact-data, budget, and conditional-auditor tests pass |
| PR-C — eval harness | Implemented | Sixteen required fixture families validate; deterministic baseline is explicitly not tuning-eligible |
| PR-D — tool policy gateway | Implemented | Role/path/action allow-ask-deny and bypass tests pass; Claude PreToolUse hook is configured |
| PR-E — provider vertical slice | Implemented locally | Claude, OpenAI, and Codex CLI adapter contracts pass; representative live record still missing |
| PR-F — risk/council engine | Implemented | Risk 0–3, independence, cross-provider, stale-diff, blocker, and adjudication tests pass |
| PR-G — tuning gate | Implemented | Contract baseline is frozen; no tuning accepted without repeated live evidence |
| PR-H — publication gate | Implemented and hardened | Manifest-owned PR metadata, shared local/GitHub policy, candidate-bound prepublication evidence, readback verification, and deterministic denial are covered |
| PR-I — release/provenance | Implemented as workflow definitions | Attestation, promotion, verification, rollback contracts pass locally; real runs are pending |
| PR-J — completion audit/freeze | Audit implemented | Freeze is blocked by the external gates below |

## External observation

The refreshed read-only GitHub observation on August 9, 2026 found a public repository and an active `Protect main` ruleset with pull requests, resolved conversations, signed commits, CodeQL, deletion/non-fast-forward protection, no bypass actors, and the required `Agent platform / contracts-policy-evals` job.

Preview, staging, and production environments exist. Production has a custom branch policy and administrator bypass is disabled, but it has no required reviewer. The `agent-evals` environment does not exist. These facts are recorded without secrets in `agent-platform/baselines/external-controls-observation-2026-08-09.json`.

Three successful subscription-authenticated Codex executions share one task fingerprint and deterministic context compilation hash. Their normalized bounded telemetry is preserved in `agent-platform/baselines/live-codex-representative-2026-08-09.json`; prompts, responses, credentials, and provider metadata are not stored. This closes the representative-run gate only. It does not create the required repeated multi-scenario comparison aggregate, and no Claude run is claimed.

## Failed hard gates

- repeated live eval baseline eligible for configuration comparison;
- non-bypassable external human-controlled production approval;
- real final-candidate signed build attestation generated and independently verified;
- real staging promotion and post-deploy verification;
- real production promotion and post-deploy verification;
- real known-good rollback drill.

A historical attestation verification and staging promotion are preserved as evidence, but staging post-deploy verification failed before the Worker-first header correction. A newer corrected build exists but has not been promoted. Neither history is substituted for the exact final closure candidate.

## Freeze rule

Do not change this page, the roadmap, or the phase status to complete/frozen until `npm run phase15:audit` passes using real reviewed evidence. Workflow definitions, synthetic adapter responses, deterministic fixtures, and unverified external settings do not satisfy live gates.
